-You were right there, Bobby.

237
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:06,061
-You were in the house.
-You were so close.

238
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:17,239
Bobby?

239
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:21,409
-You could have saved us, Bobby.
-l'm here, Bobby.

240
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:22,953
You walked right past that door.

241
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,412
[CLANGlNG]

242
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,832
-The monster had us.
-And you didn't find us.

243
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:30,418
And now, they won't find you.

244
00:19:35,258 --> 00:19:37,717
It wasn't just me, Dean.

245
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:39,594
I had a sister.

246
00:19:39,762 --> 00:19:41,096
[GRUNTS]

247
00:19:41,347 --> 00:19:43,640
A little sister.

248
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:45,433
She worshiped me.

249
00:19:46,269 --> 00:19:49,229
You know how
little siblings are, right?

250
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:52,232
How they'll do anything for you?

251
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:56,069
She was never the same
after I disappeared.

252
00:19:57,238 --> 00:19:59,114
She just--

253
00:20:00,992 --> 00:20:02,659
She just got lost.

254
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:08,623
And when my body
was lying in the morgue?

255
00:20:08,791 --> 00:20:11,751
-Beat up, broken?
-Meg.

256
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:15,297
Do you know what that did to her?
She killed herself!

257
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:17,132
Because of you, Dean.

258
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,968
Because all you were thinking about
was your family...

259
00:20:20,136 --> 00:20:22,178
...your revenge and your demons.

260
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:26,016
Fifty words of Latin a little sooner,
and l'd still be alive.

261
00:20:28,978 --> 00:20:31,980
My baby sister would still be alive.

262
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:36,902
-That blood is on your hands, Dean.
-You're right.

263
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,029
[GRUNTS]

264
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:45,201
[ICE CRACKlNG]

265
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:51,708
Bobby! Hold on, Bobby! I'm coming!

266
00:20:53,002 --> 00:20:54,336
Bobby!

267
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:58,340
[GRUNTlNG]

268
00:20:59,717 --> 00:21:00,800
Ooh.

269
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:07,349
[YELLS]

270
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:09,851
[BOTH PANTING]

271
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:13,980
[DEAN COUGHS, GROANS]

272
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:24,658
Come on, Dean.
Did your brain get french-fried in hell?

273
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:29,037
-You can't shoot me with bullets.
-l'm not shooting you.

274
00:21:37,171 --> 00:21:38,338
Iron.

275
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:40,548
[GROANS]

276
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:43,176
-So they're all people we know?
-Not just know.

277
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:45,387
People we couldn't save.

278
00:21:46,764 --> 00:21:48,056
I saw something on Meg.

279
00:21:48,224 --> 00:21:50,725
Did she have a tattoo
when she was alive?

280
00:21:50,893 --> 00:21:53,061
-l don't think so.
-Like a mark on her hand.

281
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:56,022
-Almost like a brand.
-l saw a mark too, on Henriksen.

282
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:58,733
-What did it look like?
-Paper?

283
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:00,610
Thanks.

284
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:02,195
[COCKS GUN]

285
00:22:07,535 --> 00:22:08,994
That's it.

286
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:12,622
I may have seen this before.

287
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:14,082
[LOUD THUD]

288
00:22:15,251 --> 00:22:17,752
-We gotta move. Follow me.
SAM: Oh.

289
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,255
Okay. Where are we going?

290
00:22:20,423 --> 00:22:21,756
Someplace safe, you idiot.

291
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:52,787
[THUD]

292
00:23:15,978 --> 00:23:18,980
-Bobby, is this--?
-Solid iron.

293
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:22,650
Completely coated in salt.
One hundred percent ghost-proof.

294
00:23:23,569 --> 00:23:26,112
You built a panic room?

295
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:27,572
I had a weekend off.

296
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:31,326
DEAN: Bobby?
-What?

297
00:23:32,578 --> 00:23:34,829
You're awesome.

298
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:38,625
[LAUGHS]

299
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:40,835
Oh.

300
00:23:58,479 --> 00:24:00,313
This is why I can't get behind God.

301
00:24:01,357 --> 00:24:03,525
-What are you talking about?
-lf he doesn't exist, fine.

302
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:06,319
Bad crap happens to good people,
that's how it is.

303
00:24:06,487 --> 00:24:10,532
And no rhyme or reason,
just random, horrible, evil.

304
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:12,534
I get it. Okay? l can roll with that.

305
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:16,037
But if he is out there,
what's wrong with him?

306
00:24:16,205 --> 00:24:20,542
Where the hell is he while these decent
people are getting torn to shreds?

307
00:24:20,709 --> 00:24:24,629
How does he live with himself,
you know? Why doesn't he help?

308
00:24:28,551 --> 00:24:31,761
I ain't touching this one
with a 1 0-foot pole.

309
00:24:31,929 --> 00:24:34,055
-Found it.
-What?

310
00:24:34,223 --> 00:24:38,226
The symbol you saw.
The brand on the ghosts.

311
00:24:38,394 --> 00:24:40,645
-Mark of the Witness.
SAM: Witness?

312
00:24:41,355 --> 00:24:44,023
-Witness to what?
-The unnatural.

313
00:24:44,191 --> 00:24:47,360
None of them died
what you'd call ordinary deaths.

314
00:24:47,528 --> 00:24:50,947
See, these ghosts,
they were forced to rise.

315
00:24:51,157 --> 00:24:53,950
They woke up in agony.
They're like rabid dogs.

316
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:58,746
It ain't their fault.
Someone rose them on purpose.

317
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:01,875
-Who?
-Do l look like I know?

318
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:06,588
But whoever it was
used a spell so powerful it left a mark.

319
00:25:06,755 --> 00:25:07,964
A brand on their souls.

320
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:13,553
Whoever did this had big plans.

321
00:25:13,721 --> 00:25:15,930
It's called
the Rising of the Witnesses.

322
00:25:16,098 --> 00:25:19,100
-lt figures into an ancient prophecy.
-Wait, wait.

323
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:20,810
What book is that prophecy from?

324
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:25,273
Well, the widely distributed version's
just for tourists, you know.

325
00:25:25,441 --> 00:25:28,276
But long story short: Revelations.

326
00:25:30,613 --> 00:25:32,780
This is a sign, boys.

327
00:25:34,992 --> 00:25:37,118
[IN UNlSON]
A sign of what?

328
00:25:42,458 --> 00:25:44,459
The apocalypse.

329
00:25:58,515 --> 00:26:00,475
-Apocalypse.
-Yep.

330
00:26:00,643 --> 00:26:04,771
As in "apocalypse" apocalypse?
The four horsemen, pestilence...

331
00:26:04,939 --> 00:26:08,191
-...$5-a-gallon-gas apocalypse?
-That's the one.

332
00:26:08,984 --> 00:26:12,487
The Rise of the Witnesses
is a mile marker.

333
00:26:12,655 --> 00:26:16,157
-Okay. So, what do we do now?
-Pfft. Road trip.

334
00:26:16,325 --> 00:26:21,120
Yeah. Grand Canyon,
Star Trek Experience, BunnyRanch.

335
00:26:21,288 --> 00:26:23,164
First things first.

336
00:26:23,332 --> 00:26:25,959
How about we survive
our friends out there?

337
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:29,545
Great. Any ideas, aside from staying
in this room until Judgment Day?

338
00:26:30,673 --> 00:26:34,968
It's a spell to send the witnesses
back to rest.

339
00:26:35,678 --> 00:26:37,512
-Should work.
-"Should"? Ha. Great.

340
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:42,183
If l translated correctly. I think I got
everything we need here at the house.

341
00:26:42,351 --> 00:26:45,019
Any chance you got everything
we need here in this room?

342
00:26:45,187 --> 00:26:48,523
So you thought our luck was gonna start
now all of a sudden?

343
00:26:48,691 --> 00:26:52,360
Spell's gotta be cast
over an open fire.

344
00:26:53,070 --> 00:26:56,364
-Heh. Fireplace in the library.
-Bingo.

345
00:26:57,658 --> 00:27:02,453
It's just not as appealing
as a ghost-proof panic room, you know?

346
00:27:04,164 --> 00:27:05,665
[EXHALES]

347
00:27:06,709 --> 00:27:08,209
[GUN COCKS]

348
00:27:12,214 --> 00:27:15,842
Cover each other, and aim careful.

349
00:27:16,010 --> 00:27:20,179
Don't run out of ammo until l'm done,
or they'll shred you.

350
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:21,764
Ready?

351
00:27:26,729 --> 00:27:28,229
[THUD]

352
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:03,264
Hey, Dean. You remember me?

353
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:07,310
Everybody on the floor, now!

354
00:28:10,773 --> 00:28:13,399
-He's got the laser eyes.
-Ronald?

355
00:28:13,567 --> 00:28:15,526
Huh? With the laser eyes?

356
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:20,406
-l wish l could say it's good to see you.
-l am dead because of you.

357
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:25,036
You were supposed to help me.

358
00:28:27,956 --> 00:28:30,917
If you're gonna shoot, shoot.
Don't talk.

359
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:50,645
Upstairs. Linen closet. Red hex box.

360
00:28:50,813 --> 00:28:53,314
-lt'll be heavy.
-Got it.

361
00:28:58,821 --> 00:28:59,821
Bobby.

362
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:07,995
[GlRLS GlGGLING]

363
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:11,833
Kitchen. Cutlery drawer.
It's got a false bottom.

364
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:15,002
Hemlock, opium, wormwood.

365
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:18,172
-Opium?
-Go.

366
00:29:19,675 --> 00:29:23,678
Bobby. You walked right by us...

367
00:29:23,846 --> 00:29:26,681
...while that monster ate us all up.

368
00:29:26,849 --> 00:29:28,307
You could've saved us.

369
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:37,650
[THUD]

370
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:56,544
MEG: You know what really
pisses me off, Sam?

371
00:29:56,712 --> 00:29:58,754
You saw how I suffered, for months.

372
00:29:59,882 --> 00:30:02,508
I thought you must
have learned something.

373
00:30:04,386 --> 00:30:06,721
-l thought l died for something.
-Meg.

374
00:30:06,889 --> 00:30:09,348
But what you're doing
with that demon, Ruby?

375
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:17,732
How many innocent bodies
has Ruby burned through for kicks?

376
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:21,027
How many girls just like me?

377
00:30:21,195 --> 00:30:23,946
And you don't send her back to hell?

378
00:30:24,156 --> 00:30:25,406
You're a monster.

379
00:30:36,418 --> 00:30:38,461
-Dean?
-l'm all right, Bobby. Keep working.

380
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:45,551
[GASPS]

381
00:30:46,929 --> 00:30:48,221
[DRAWER CLOSES]

382
00:30:48,764 --> 00:30:50,932
-Victor.
-Dean.

383
00:30:52,226 --> 00:30:54,727
-l know.
-No, you don't.

384
00:30:55,938 --> 00:30:59,482
It's my fault you're dead.
I left you behind.

385
00:30:59,691 --> 00:31:03,569
And the minute l heard
about that explosion, l thought....

386
00:31:03,737 --> 00:31:08,324
I should've known.
I should've protected you.

387
00:31:10,202 --> 00:31:13,329
Nuh-uh. Not so fast.

388
00:31:15,123 --> 00:31:17,500
You think you left, then Lilith came...

389
00:31:17,709 --> 00:31:21,587
...and we all died in a beautiful blast
of white light?

390
00:31:22,756 --> 00:31:23,798
If only.

391
00:31:25,342 --> 00:31:28,135
Forty-five minutes.

392
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:31,180
-What?
-Over 45 minutes.

393
00:31:31,348 --> 00:31:34,100
Lilith said she wanted
to have some fun.

394
00:31:34,643 --> 00:31:39,021
The secretary was first.
Remember her? Nancy? The virgin?

395
00:31:39,231 --> 00:31:43,317
Lilith flayed Nancy's skin off,
piece by piece.

396
00:31:43,485 --> 00:31:46,112
Right in front of us.
Made us watch.

397
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:49,323
-Nancy never stopped screaming.
-No.

398
00:31:49,491 --> 00:31:51,993
I was the last.

399
00:31:55,289 --> 00:31:56,330
Victor, l'm--

400
00:31:56,498 --> 00:31:58,624
[GRUNTlNG]

401
00:32:00,377 --> 00:32:03,671
Tell me how it's fair.
You get saved from hell, l die?

402
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:06,674
Why do you deserve
another chance, Dean?

403
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:14,890
[GASPS, GROANS]

404
00:32:16,018 --> 00:32:18,894
-You all right?
-No.

405
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:21,147
-Let's go. Come on.
-Uhn!

406
00:32:31,700 --> 00:32:34,702
Ronald. Hey, come on, man.

407
00:32:34,870 --> 00:32:37,872
-l thought we were pals.
-That's when l was breathing.

408
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:39,874
Now I'm gonna eat you alive.

409
00:32:40,042 --> 00:32:41,876
Heh-heh. Well....

410
00:32:42,044 --> 00:32:44,420
Come on. l'm not a cheeseburger.

411
00:32:50,010 --> 00:32:52,803
[CHANTING lN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

412
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:04,398
[BOBBY RESUMES CHANTING]

413
00:33:12,532 --> 00:33:14,033
Sam!

414
00:33:48,652 --> 00:33:50,069
[GUN CLlCKS]

415
00:34:01,164 --> 00:34:02,498
[GRUNTlNG]

416
00:34:03,959 --> 00:34:05,960
-Sam!
-Cover Bobby.

417
00:34:17,931 --> 00:34:19,098
[SCREAMS]

418
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:27,314
BOBBY:
Dean.

419
00:34:29,192 --> 00:34:31,026
-Fireplace.
-Aah!

420
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:38,492
Aah.

421
00:34:38,660 --> 00:34:40,411
[BOBBY GASPS]

422
00:34:42,497 --> 00:34:44,165
Bobby.

423
00:34:46,668 --> 00:34:48,127
[GRUNTS]

424
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:50,671
[WHEEZES, PANTING]

425
00:35:13,195 --> 00:35:15,237
[WlNGS RUSTLlNG]

426
00:35:46,853 --> 00:35:48,479
Excellent job with the witnesses.

427
00:35:49,689 --> 00:35:52,983
-You were hip to all this?
-l was, uh, made aware.

428
00:35:54,110 --> 00:35:56,737
Well, thanks a lot
for the angelic assistance.

429
00:35:56,905 --> 00:35:59,573
You know, I almost got my heart
ripped out of my chest.

430
00:35:59,741 --> 00:36:01,116
But you didn't.

431
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:04,203
I thought angels
were supposed to be guardians.

432
00:36:04,913 --> 00:36:09,375
Fluffy wings, halos....
You know, Michael Landon.

433
00:36:09,543 --> 00:36:10,751
Not dicks.

434
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:17,258
Read the Bible.
Angels are warriors of God.

435
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:19,760
-l'm a soldier.
-Yeah? Then why didn't you fight?

436
00:36:20,762 --> 00:36:24,723
I'm not here
to perch on your shoulder.

437
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:27,393
-We had larger concerns.
-Concerns?

438
00:36:28,562 --> 00:36:31,063
There were people getting
torn to shreds down here.

439
00:36:31,231 --> 00:36:33,399
And by the way,
while all this is going on...

440
00:36:33,567 --> 00:36:36,610
...where the hell is your boss,
huh, if there is a God?

441
00:36:36,778 --> 00:36:39,071
-There's a God.
-l'm not convinced.

442
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:44,451
Because if there's a God,
what the hell is he waiting for?

443
00:36:44,619 --> 00:36:48,330
Genocide? Monsters roaming the earth?
The freaking apocalypse?

444
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:50,583
At what point
does he lift a damn finger...

445
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:52,960
...and help the poor bastards
stuck down here?

446
00:36:53,128 --> 00:36:54,169
The Lord works--

447
00:36:54,337 --> 00:36:57,965
If you say "mysterious ways,"
so help me, I will kick your ass.

448
00:37:04,639 --> 00:37:07,141
So Bobby was right...

449
00:37:07,976 --> 00:37:09,977
...about the witnesses?

450
00:37:10,478 --> 00:37:14,148
Was this some kind of a sign
of the apocalypse?

451
00:37:14,316 --> 00:37:17,610
That's why we're here.
Big things afoot.

452
00:37:17,777 --> 00:37:20,279
Do I wanna know
what kind of things?

453
00:37:20,447 --> 00:37:23,699
I sincerely doubt it,
but you need to know.

454
00:37:24,659 --> 00:37:28,662
The Rising of the Witnesses
is one of the 66 seals.

455
00:37:28,830 --> 00:37:30,956
I'm guessing that's not a show
at SeaWorld.

456
00:37:31,124 --> 00:37:35,502
Those seals are being broken by Lilith.

457
00:37:39,132 --> 00:37:40,841
She did the spell,
she rose the witnesses?

458
00:37:41,009 --> 00:37:44,136
Mm-hm. And not just here.

459
00:37:44,304 --> 00:37:46,555
-Twenty other hunters are dead.
-Of course.

460
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:48,891
She picked victims
the hunters couldn't save.

461
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:51,185
So that they would
barrel right after us.

462
00:37:51,353 --> 00:37:55,022
-Lilith has a certain sense of humor.
-We put those spirits back to rest.

463
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:57,524
Doesn't matter. The seal was broken.

464
00:37:58,401 --> 00:38:00,736
Why break the seal, anyway?

465
00:38:00,904 --> 00:38:03,155
You think of the seals
as locks on a door.

466
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:06,033
Okay. Last one opens and...?

467
00:38:11,206 --> 00:38:13,165
Lucifer walks free.

468
00:38:18,171 --> 00:38:19,922
Lucifer?

469
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:24,885
I thought Lucifer was just a story
they told at demon Sunday school.

470
00:38:25,053 --> 00:38:26,261
There's no such thing.

471
00:38:26,763 --> 00:38:29,723
Three days ago, you thought
there was no such thing as me.

472
00:38:33,228 --> 00:38:35,729
Why do you think we're here,
walking among you now...

473
00:38:35,897 --> 00:38:38,232
...for the first time in 2000 years?

474
00:38:40,068 --> 00:38:41,276
To stop Lucifer.

475
00:38:43,196 --> 00:38:45,072
It's why we've arrived.

476
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:51,912
Well, bang-up job so far.

477
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:55,082
Stellar work with the witnesses.
It's nice.

478
00:38:57,419 --> 00:38:59,795
We tried.

479
00:39:00,422 --> 00:39:02,715
There are other battles.

480
00:39:02,882 --> 00:39:06,093
Other seals.
Some we'll win, some we'll lose.

481
00:39:06,261 --> 00:39:07,803
This one we lost.

482
00:39:07,971 --> 00:39:09,388
[SCOFFS]

483
00:39:12,392 --> 00:39:15,310
Our numbers are not unlimited.

484
00:39:16,980 --> 00:39:20,149
Six of my brothers died
in the field this week.

485
00:39:20,316 --> 00:39:25,279
You think the armies of heaven
should just follow you around?

486
00:39:26,197 --> 00:39:28,741
There's a bigger picture here.

487
00:39:32,954 --> 00:39:35,581
You should show me some respect.

488
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:41,628
I dragged you out of hell.
I can throw you back in.

489
00:39:48,845 --> 00:39:50,304
[GASPS]

490
00:40:01,858 --> 00:40:04,651
Ha. You all right?

491
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:07,654
What's wrong, Dean?

492
00:40:09,741 --> 00:40:14,328
So, ahem,
you got no problem believing...

493
00:40:14,496 --> 00:40:15,871
...in God and angels?

494
00:40:17,499 --> 00:40:19,458
No, not really.

495
00:40:22,337 --> 00:40:25,005
So l guess that means
you believe in the devil.

496
00:40:26,466 --> 00:40:28,759
Why are you asking me all this?

497
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:09,716
[ENGLISH SDH]

